                                                                                     rdfs:label "public sector001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#responsible001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#responsible001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                            <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Responsible_for_treatment_in_verification> ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#is_compliant_with_the_following_roles> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#responsible001> ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Analysis_methodologies> "Places analysis methodologies" ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Binding_cooperative_rules> "The person in charge and the person responsible are responsible for the application of binding cooperative rules." ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Contract> "It is present in the process of signing a contract, it can also be present in the process of signing a contract, these same functions have the data processor in the present law." ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Details_of_the_law_details> "Information" ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#General_detail> "It performs the transfer, verification and security processes on the owner's data." ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Impact_assessment> "The data controller is responsible for carrying out the impact assessment." ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Implementing_verification_processes> "Implements verification processes" ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Maintaining_the_accuracy_of_the_information> "The person in charge and the person in charge are responsible for maintaining the accuracy of the information in the transfer and verification processes." ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Members_of_the_protection_system_details> "General information" ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Name> "Carla" ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Obligations_of_the_responsible_person_and_manager> "Perform transfer and verification processes, apply processes, use methodologies and take technological measures." ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Perform_evaluations> "Evaluates what the manager does" ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Personal_data_security_details> "The person in charge and responsible for personal data is responsible for ensuring the security of the owner's data." ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Personal_detail> "It is responsible for the processing of the holder's personal data and for the authorization to carry out international transfers." ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Personal_information> "Information about the responsible party" ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Protection_policies> "Establishes data protection policies" ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Safety_from_design_by_defect> "You must implement security from the default design in the data." ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Security_notification_of_infringement> "The person in charge is responsible for notifying in the event of a security leak." ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Self-regulation> "Data controllers and processors must adhere to codes of conduct, seals, certifications and protection marks, without this constituting an exemption from the responsibility to comply with the provisions of this law, its regulations, guidelines and regulations issued by the Personal Data Protection Authority." ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Serious> """These violations are commensurate with the data controller's infraction or misconduct.
For example, failure to implement administrative measures.""" ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Slight> """These infractions are in accordance with the infraction or fault of the data controller.
For example, failure to process or implement a process in the transfer of information would be considered a minor infraction.""" ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Very_serious> "Not specified, but if there is, the Authority decides what action to take." ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Violations_in_verification> "Faults in their actions" ;
                                                                                   rdfs:label "responsible001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#right_of_deletion001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#right_of_deletion001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                  <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Right_of_deletion_in_verification> ;
                                                                                         <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#can_be_rights_of> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#right_of_deletion001> ;
                                                                                         <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Consent_in_verification> "Must be consented to by the owner" ;
                                                                                         <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#General_detail> "This right talks about the scenarios in which the owner of the information can delete his/her data and for this purpose he/she has a period of 15 days." ;
                                                                                         <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Informed> "It can be an informed consent" ;
                                                                                         <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Not_informed> "It can be an informed consent" ;
                                                                                         <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Purpose> "To delete data, it must have a purpose." ;
                                                                                         <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Revoke_consent> "It must be possible to revoke the consent at any time, this can be done by the owner of the data." ;
                                                                                         <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Updated> "Must be updated" ;
                                                                                         <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#time_of_right_to_elimination> "15 days" ;
                                                                                         rdfs:label "right of deletion001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#right_to_correct_and_update001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#right_to_correct_and_update001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                            <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Right_to_correct_and_update_in_verification> ;
                                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#can_be_rights_of> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#right_to_correct_and_update001> ;
                                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Consent_in_verification> "Must be consented to by the owner" ;
                                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#General_detail> "This right states that the owner of the information has the possibility to update their data when it is inaccurate or incomplete, and this must be done within 15 days." ;
                                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Informed> "It can be an informed consent" ;
                                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Not_informed> "May be an uninformed consent" ;
                                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Preservation_time> "The time is 15 days" ;
                                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Revoke_consent> "It must be possible to revoke the consent at any time, this can be done by the owner of the data." ;
                                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Scope_of_credit_rights> "In the credit rights it is stipulated that such rights, as well as all the rights present in the law, have the option of a rectification of information in case the holder needs it." ;
                                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Updated> "Must be updated" ;
                                                                                                   rdfs:label "right to correct and update001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#right_to_portability001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#right_to_portability001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                     <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Right_to_portability> ;
                                                                                            <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#can_be_rights_of> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#right_to_portability001> ;
                                                                                            <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Compatible> "Must be compatible" ;
                                                                                            <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Consent_in_verification> "Must be consented to by the owner" ;
                                                                                            <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#General_detail> "This right talks about how the holder can request the transfer of his data to another person or responsible when the situation warrants it and for this right there is no established time." ;
                                                                                            <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Gratuity> "Must be free of charge for the holder" ;
                                                                                            <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Informed> "It can be an informed consent" ;
                                                                                            <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Not_informed> "May be an uninformed consent" ;
                                                                                            <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Revoke_consent> "It must be possible to revoke the consent at any time, this can be done by the owner of the data." ;
                                                                                            <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Structured> "Must be structured" ;
                                                                                            <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Updated> "Must be updated" ;
                                                                                            rdfs:label "right to portability001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#right_to_the_information001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#right_to_the_information001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                         <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Right_to_information_in_verification> ;
                                                                                                <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#can_be_rights_of> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#right_to_the_information001> ;
                                                                                                <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Consent_in_verification> "Must be consented to by the owner" ;
                                                                                                <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Data_use> "The owner's data must be free from use in information automation processes, in order to avoid automated decisions on any specific subject." ;
                                                                                                <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#General_detail> "This right means that the owner of the data must know what is going to be done with them and how they are going to be treated either in the field of data processing or in the field of transfer of information, and to complete this task there is a period of 30 days." ;
                                                                                                <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Informed> "Puede ser un consentimiento informado" ;
                                                                                                <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Not_informed> "May be an uninformed consent" ;
                                                                                                <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Preservation_time> "It has 30 days to inform the holder that his data was obtained in a non-direct way, this is done by the responsible and in charge." ;
                                                                                                <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Revoke_consent> "It must be possible to revoke the consent at any time, this can be done by the owner of the data." ;
                                                                                                <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Updated> "The information must be up to date" ;
                                                                                                rdfs:label "right to the information001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#rights001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#rights001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Rights_in_verification> ;
                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#the_law_has_the_following_rights> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#rights001> ;
                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Rights_in_verification> "Rights of the holder before the law" ;
                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#exceptions_to_rights> "Exceptions to the rights, cases in which the holder's data can be used without his/her consent." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "rights001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#sanctioning_regime001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#sanctioning_regime001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Sanctioning_regime> ;
                                                                                          <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#the_verification_covers_aspects_such_as> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#sanctioning_regime001> ;
                                                                                          <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#General_detail> "These are the consequences to which the entities involved in the law are prone to. Verify that everything is working correctly and if not, a penalty is applied." ;
                                                                                          <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Precautionary_measures> "Precautionary measures" ;
                                                                                          <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Sanctioning_administrative_procedure> "Actions in case of a bad practice in the use of data" ;
                                                                                          rdfs:label "sanctioning regime001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#security_from_design001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#security_from_design001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                     <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Follow-up_from_design> ;
                                                                                            <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#account_with_actions_as> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#security_from_design001> ;
                                                                                            <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#General_detail> "It is the initial protection to which the data is subject and it is the responsibility of the data controller to apply it." ;
                                                                                            <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Safety_from_design_by_defect> "Data must be subject to security by design by default" ;
                                                                                            rdfs:label "security from design001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#sensitive_data001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#sensitive_data001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                               <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Sensitive_data_in_verification> ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#that_can_be> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#sensitive_data001> ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Access> "They must have optimal access" ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Anonymization> "Data must be anonymized" ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Correction> "It must be possible to rectify" ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Disposal> "It should be possible to eliminate" ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Updated> "The data must be up to date" ;
                                                                                      rdfs:label "sensitive data001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#solve_an_urgence001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#solve_an_urgence001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Solve_an_emergency> ;
                                                                                        <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#segmented_into_the_following_national_cases> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#solve_an_urgence001> ;
                                                                                        <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Anonymization> "A nationwide transfer can be forced when an emergency is expected to be solved and must be anonymous." ;
                                                                                        <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Exceptions> "A transfer can be forced at the national level when an emergency is expected to be solved" ;
                                                                                        <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#General_detail> "This exception indicates that in the event of a vital emergency, the owner's data may be used without the owner's consent." ;
                                                                                        rdfs:label "solve an urgence001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#sources_accessible_to_the_public001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#sources_accessible_to_the_public001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Sources_accessible_to_the_public> ;
                                                                                                        <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#segmented_into_the_following_national_cases> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#sources_accessible_to_the_public001> ;
                                                                                                        <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Exceptions> "At the national level, the sources must be accessible to the public." ;
                                                                                                        <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#General_detail> "The holder's data may be used as long as the information is present in public sources. For example, public databases." ;
                                                                                                        rdfs:label "sources accessible to the public001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#specific_consent001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#specific_consent001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
                                                                                        <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#can_be> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#specific_consent001> ;
                                                                                        <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Informed> "When any specific consent is requested from the data subject" ;
                                                                                        <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Not_informed> "When no specific consent is requested from the data subject." ;
                                                                                        rdfs:label "specific consent001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#techniques001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#techniques001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                           <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Techniques> ;
                                                                                  <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#that_can_be_of_the_type> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#techniques001> ;
                                                                                  <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Applied> "When the verification process is applied" ;
                                                                                  <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Cessation_of_treatment> "When the corrective action stops" ;
                                                                                  <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#General_detail> "Technical corrective actions, e.g., error corrections in information transfer events." ;
                                                                                  <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Guidelines> "Guidelines for a technical process" ,
                                                                                                                                                                 "Technical guidelines" ;
                                                                                  <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Not_applied> "When the verification process does not apply" ;
                                                                                  <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Regulations> "Technical regulations" ;
                                                                                  <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Technical_measurements> "Measures for a technical verification process" ;
                                                                                  rdfs:label "techniques001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#teenagers001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#teenagers001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                          <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Teenagers> ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#and_as_your_age_will_have_to_be_of_your_age> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#teenagers001> ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Access> "Adolescent data must be accessible" ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Anonymization> "It must be possible to anonymize adolescent data." ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Correction> "Adolescent data must be able to be rectified" ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Disposal> "It should be possible to delete teenage data" ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#General_detail> "In order to make use of their data, no detailed supervision is necessary, only the use to which the data will be put needs to be clearly stated. The age range to be considered as adolescent data is from 12 to 17 years old." ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Supervision> "Teenagers can use their personal information without the need for adult consent, they do not need supervision, but the use that will be made of their data must be very clear." ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Updated> "Adolescent data must be updatable" ;
                                                                                 rdfs:label "teenagers001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#transfer_or_communication001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#transfer_or_communication001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                          <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Transfer_or_communication> ;
                                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#has_elements_of_transfer_and_communication> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#transfer_or_communication001> ;
                                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Certifying_international_transfer_processes> "Approve the transfer processes when these are clear" ;
                                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Contract> "Contract with stakeholders" ;
                                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Data_admitted_countries_international_transfer> "Admitted countries information" ;
                                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Detail_transfer_domestic_domestic_scope> "Information" ;
                                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Exceptions> "Exceptions that may occur in the transfer process" ;
                                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Informed> "Rights informed" ;
                                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Legal_or_regulatory_obligation> "Legal obligations" ;
                                                                                                 rdfs:label "transfer or communication001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#treatment001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#treatment001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                          <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Treatment_Manager_in_verification> ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#is_compliant_with_the_following_roles> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#treatment001> ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Analysis_methodologies> "Analysis methodology to be used on the data" ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Binding_cooperative_rules> "The person in charge and the person responsible are responsible for the application of binding cooperative rules." ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Details_of_the_law_details> "Information" ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#General_detail> "It performs the same activities as the data controller in terms of transfer, verification and security." ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Implementing_verification_processes> "Must implement data verification processes" ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Maintaining_the_accuracy_of_the_information> "The person in charge and the person in charge are responsible for maintaining the accuracy of the information in the transfer and verification processes." ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Members_of_the_protection_system_details> "Information indicating that it is part of the law" ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Name> "Ana" ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#National_registry_for_the_protection_of_personal_data> "Records data information" ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Obligations_of_the_responsible_person_and_manager> "Apply processes, implement protection policies, use methodologies and take technological measures" ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Perform_evaluations> "It is responsible for conducting evaluations" ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Personal_data_security_details> "The person in charge and responsible for personal data is responsible for ensuring the security of the owner's data." ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Personal_detail> "It is in charge of data processing and transfer processes when its assistance is required." ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Personal_information> "Personal information of the person in charge" ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Protection_policies> "Data protection policies to be applied to the data" ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Safety_from_design_by_defect> "Security must be in place from the beginning of the data processing." ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Self-regulation> "Data controllers and processors must adhere to codes of conduct, seals, certifications and protection marks, without this constituting an exemption from the responsibility to comply with the provisions of this law, its regulations, guidelines and regulations issued by the Personal Data Protection Authority." ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Serious> """These infractions are in accordance with the infraction or fault of the person responsible for the data.
For example, if an administrative procedure is not carried out.""" ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Slight> """These infractions are in accordance with the infraction or fault of the data controller.
For example, failure to process or implement a process in the transfer of information would be considered a minor infraction.""" ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Very_serious> "Not specified, but if there is, the Authority decides what action to take." ;
                                                                                 rdfs:label "treatment001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#unequivocal_consent001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#unequivocal_consent001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
                                                                                           <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#can_be> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#unequivocal_consent001> ;
                                                                                           <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Informed> "When any unambiguous consent is requested from the data subject" ;
                                                                                           <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Not_informed> "When unambiguous consent is not requested from the data subject" ;
                                                                                           rdfs:label "unequivocal consent001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#verification001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#verification001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Verification> ;
                                                                                    <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#a_process_of> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#verification001> ;
                                                                                    <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Audit> "Verification processes should be audited when necessary." ;
                                                                                    <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Audit_detail> "Information on the audit performed" ;
                                                                                    <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#General_detail> "They are misuses of the information by the people who had contact with the data." ;
                                                                                    rdfs:label "verification001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#violation_investigation001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#violation_investigation001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                        <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Infringement_investigation> ;
                                                                                               <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#segmented_into_the_following_international_cases> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#violation_investigation001> ;
                                                                                               <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Detail_of_investigation_of_infringements> "If the data subject has breach information, he/she is subject to an international exception on his/her data." ;
                                                                                               <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#General_detail> "When the owner of the information has committed an offense or committed a crime, this information may be investigated without the owner's consent." ;
                                                                                               rdfs:label "violation investigation001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#vital_interest_in_another_person001
<http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#vital_interest_in_another_person001> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Vital_interest_of_another_person> ;
                                                                                                        <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#segmented_into_the_following_international_cases> <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#vital_interest_in_another_person001> ;
                                                                                                        <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#General_detail> "When the data subject is unable to consent to the use of the data." ;
                                                                                                        <http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Vital_interest_detail_of_another_person> "Research for a critical disease" ;
                                                                                                        rdfs:label "vital interest in another person001" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Members_of_the_personal_data_protection_system
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Members_of_the_personal_data_protection_system> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Members_of_the_personal_data_protection_system> ;
                                                                                                                     <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#are_composed_of> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#data_owner> ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                           <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#data_processor> ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                           <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#delegate> ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                           <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#personal_data_protection_authority> ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                           <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#recipient> ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                           <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#responsible_for_treatment> ;
                                                                                                                     <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#description> "They are all those persons who participate in the Personal Data Protection Law." .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Purpose
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Purpose> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Purpose> ;
                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#is_distinct_from_data_collection_in_the> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#data_processing> ;
                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#description> "Personal data may not be processed for purposes other than those established at the time of collection, unless the conditions permitting further processing as set forth in the Organic Law on the Protection of Personal Data are met." ;
                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#shall_be> "Communicated to the owner of the data, therefore, the owner of the data must be informed in a clear and understandable manner about the purposes of the processing, so that he/she can make informed decisions about the use of his/her personal data." ,
                                                                                                                                                             "Determined, i.e., they must be specific and well defined, without ambiguity, so that it is clear what will be done with the data collected." ,
                                                                                                                                                             "Explicit, i.e. they must be transparent and easily understandable for the data subject, without leaving room for confusing interpretations." ,
                                                                                                                                                             "Legitimate, which means that they must be based on valid legal grounds and comply with data protection regulations." .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#anonymization
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#anonymization> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Anonymization> ;
                                                                                    <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#description> "The implementation of measures to prevent the identification or re-identification of a natural person shall be carried out without incurring disproportionate efforts. This implies that privacy-preserving actions shall be taken without requiring excessive resources, time or effort that are not justified by the benefits or purpose pursued." ;
                                                                                    rdfs:comment "The implementation of measures to prevent the identification or re-identification of a natural person shall be carried out without incurring disproportionate efforts. This implies that privacy-preserving actions shall be taken without requiring excessive resources, time or effort that are not justified by the benefits or purpose pursued."@en ,
                                                                                                 "The implementation of measures to prevent the identification or re-identification of a natural person shall be carried out without incurring disproportionate efforts. This implies that privacy-preserving actions shall be taken without requiring excessive resources, time or effort that are not justified by the benefits or purpose pursued."@es ;
                                                                                    rdfs:label "anonymization" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#anonymized_data
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#anonymized_data> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                               <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Anonymized_data> ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#explanation_of_concept_of_inapplicability> "As soon as the data is no longer anonymized or anonymized, its processing will be subject to compliance with the obligations of this Law, especially the obligation to have a lawful basis for continuing to process the data in a non-anonymized or non-anonymized manner." ;
                                                                                      rdfs:label "anonymized data" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#applicability
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#applicability> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Applicability> ;
                                                                                    <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#scope_of_legislation> "La Ley Orgánica de Protección de Datos Personales se aplicará en ciertos escenarios" ;
                                                                                    rdfs:label "applicability" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#application_favorable_to_the_owner
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#application_favorable_to_the_owner> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                                  <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Application_favorable_to_the_owner> ;
                                                                                                         <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#description> "In situations where there is uncertainty as to how to interpret and apply the legal or contractual provisions related to the protection of personal data, judicial and administrative officials must opt for the interpretation that benefits the owner of such data, i.e., the owner must be favored in terms of protection and safeguarding of his personal data in case of ambiguity or doubt in the application of the Organic Law for the Protection of Personal Data." ;
                                                                                                         rdfs:comment "In situations where there is uncertainty as to how to interpret and apply the legal or contractual provisions related to the protection of personal data, judicial and administrative officials must opt for the interpretation that benefits the owner of such data, i.e., the owner must be favored in terms of protection and safeguarding of his personal data in case of ambiguity or doubt in the application of the Organic Law for the Protection of Personal Data."@en ,
                                                                                                                      "In situations where there is uncertainty as to how to interpret and apply the legal or contractual provisions related to the protection of personal data, judicial and administrative officials must opt for the interpretation that benefits the owner of such data, i.e., the owner must be favored in terms of protection and safeguarding of his personal data in case of ambiguity or doubt in the application of the Organic Law for the Protection of Personal Data."@es ;
                                                                                                         rdfs:label "application favorable to the owner" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#biometric_data
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#biometric_data> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Biometric_data> ;
                                                                                     <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#description> "Unique personal data, related to the physical or physiological characteristics, or behaviors of a natural person that allows or confirms the unique identification of such person, such as facial images or fingerprint data, among others." ;
                                                                                     rdfs:comment "Unique personal data, related to the physical or physiological characteristics, or behaviors of a natural person that allows or confirms the unique identification of such person, such as facial images or fingerprint data, among others."@en ,
                                                                                                  "Unique personal data, related to the physical or physiological characteristics, or behaviors of a natural person that allows or confirms the unique identification of such person, such as facial images or fingerprint data, among others."@es ;
                                                                                     rdfs:label "biometric data" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#certifying_entity
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#certifying_entity> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Certifying_entity> ;
                                                                                        <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#is_authorized_by> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#personal_data_protection_authority> ;
                                                                                        <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#description> "Entity that has the capacity to issue certifications in the area of personal data protection, in a non-exclusive manner, which means that it is not the only entity with this power, and other organizations may also grant certifications in the same area." ;
                                                                                        rdfs:comment "Entity that has the capacity to issue certifications in the area of personal data protection, in a non-exclusive manner, which means that it is not the only entity with this power, and other organizations may also grant certifications in the same area."@en ,
                                                                                                     "Entity that has the capacity to issue certifications in the area of personal data protection, in a non-exclusive manner, which means that it is not the only entity with this power, and other organizations may also grant certifications in the same area."@es ;
                                                                                        rdfs:label "certifying entity" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#claims
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#claims> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Claims> ;
                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#are_destined_to> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#responsible_for_treatment> ;
                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#may_be_made_by> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#data_owner> ;
                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#answer_the_claim> "The responsible party must respond to the request within 10 days, either with an affirmative or negative answer, notifying and executing the corresponding actions." ;
                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#before_answering_the_claim> "The Personal Data Protection Authority may carry out actions including preliminary investigations, information gathering and evaluation of the circumstances of the case, in accordance with the provisions of the Organic Administrative Code." ;
                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#claims_of> "Claims related to the exercise of the holder's rights in the processing of personal data" ,
                                                                                                                                                             "Complaints related to compliance with obligations of the data controller" ,
                                                                                                                                                             "Complaints related to the application of principles in data processing" ;
                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#in_the_face_of_a_denial_or_no_response_to_the_claim> "The data subject may bring civil, criminal or constitutional actions as deemed necessary." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                       "The holder may file an administrative complaint with the Personal Data Protection Authority." ;
                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#may_be_done_by_means> "Digitals" ,
                                                                                                                                                                        "Physicists" ;
                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#may_be_made_in_shape> "Free" ;
                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#submit_in_case_of_claim> "Presentar quejas" ,
                                                                                                                                                                           "Submit petitions" ,
                                                                                                                                                                           "Submit requirements" ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "claims" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#collection
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#collection> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                          <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Collection> ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#is_related_to> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#consent> ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#need_of> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#consent> ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#description> "Refers to the process of acquiring and obtaining data from various sources, such as sensors, databases, online forms, historical records, among others." ;
                                                                                 rdfs:comment "Refers to the process of acquiring and obtaining data from various sources, such as sensors, databases, online forms, historical records, among others."@en ,
                                                                                              "Refers to the process of acquiring and obtaining data from various sources, such as sensors, databases, online forms, historical records, among others."@es ;
                                                                                 rdfs:label "collection" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#confidentiality
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#confidentiality> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                               <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Confidentiality> ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#description> "Information obtained from the processing of personal data must be handled with care and kept secret. This means that the information should not be used or shared for purposes other than those for which it was collected, unless there are special circumstances permitted by law that justify further processing of the data." ;
                                                                                      rdfs:comment "Information obtained from the processing of personal data must be handled with care and kept secret. This means that the information should not be used or shared for purposes other than those for which it was collected, unless there are special circumstances permitted by law that justify further processing of the data."@en ,
                                                                                                   "Information obtained from the processing of personal data must be handled with care and kept secret. This means that the information should not be used or shared for purposes other than those for which it was collected, unless there are special circumstances permitted by law that justify further processing of the data."@es ;
                                                                                      rdfs:label "confidentiality" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#consent
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#consent> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Consent> ;
                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#in_cases_of_direct_data_gathering_by_the> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#data_owner> ;
                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#in_the_case_of_no_direct_data_collection_by_the> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#data_owner> ;
                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#is_related_to> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#consent_defects> ,
                                                                                                                                                                  <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#revocation_of_consent> ;
                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#characteristics_that_the_information_transferred_to_the_owner_must_have> "Clear, simple and easy to understand language" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                                            "Preferably, the information should be available in the language chosen by the owner." ;
                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#conditions_for_legitimate_treatment> "By consent of the owner for the processing of his personal data for one or more specific purposes." ;
                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#description> "Expression by which the owner of the personal data grants his/her authorization to the data controller to process such data." ;
                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#for_health-related_data_without_consent> "The consent of the owner shall not be required for the processing of health data." ;
                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#for_plurality_of_purposes> "It is necessary to specify that such consent is given for all the purposes for which consent is being requested." ;
                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#how_the_information_may_be_transmitted_to_the_owner> "Within any testable mode" ;
                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#to_deal_with_and_communicate_personal_data_must> "The manifestation of the holder's will to do so must be counted, i.e., when the data subject has given his/her consent for the processing or communication of personal data to occur." ;
                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#valid> "Free from defects of consent" ,
                                                                                                                                                          "Informed to ensure transparency and the right to information" ,
                                                                                                                                                          "Specific with respect to the means and purposes of processing" ,
                                                                                                                                                          "Unequivocal, no doubt about the authorization granted by the holder" ;
                                                                              rdfs:comment "Expression by which the owner of the personal data grants his/her authorization to the data controller to process such data."@en ,
                                                                                           "Expression by which the owner of the personal data grants his/her authorization to the data controller to process such data."@es ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "consent" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#consent_defects
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#consent_defects> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                               <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Consent_defects> ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#description> "They refer to situations in which the person does not fully understand what he/she is authorizing or when his/her consent is not truly free and voluntary." ;
                                                                                      rdfs:comment "They refer to situations in which the person does not fully understand what he/she is authorizing or when his/her consent is not truly free and voluntary."@en ,
                                                                                                   "They refer to situations in which the person does not fully understand what he/she is authorizing or when his/her consent is not truly free and voluntary."@es ;
                                                                                      rdfs:label "consent defects" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#conservation
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#conservation> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                            <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Conservation> ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#responsible_for_establishing_the_deadlines_for_suspension_or_periodic_review_within_data_processing_is> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#responsible_for_treatment> ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#description> "The conservation of personal data implies keeping them for a period that does not exceed the time necessary to fulfill the purpose for which they were initially collected and processed." ;
                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#extended_preservation_of_personal_data_processing> "Archival purposes in the public interest, i.e., preservation of data for archival purposes that benefit the public interest, such as preserving the historical or administrative memory of a society." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                           "Historical research purposes for the purpose of studying events, periods or aspects of the past to better understand history, the evolution of society, cultures or institutions over time." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                           "Scientific research purposes, that is, when the processing of personal data is used for scientific studies that seek to generate knowledge, understand natural or social phenomena, validate theories or contribute to the advancement of a particular discipline." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                           "Statistical research purposes with the objective of performing quantitative and qualitative analyses to understand patterns, trends and relationships in a specific population or phenomenon." ;
                                                                                   rdfs:comment "The conservation of personal data implies keeping them for a period that does not exceed the time necessary to fulfill the purpose for which they were initially collected and processed."@en ,
                                                                                                "The conservation of personal data implies keeping them for a period that does not exceed the time necessary to fulfill the purpose for which they were initially collected and processed."@es ;
                                                                                   rdfs:label "conservation" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#corrective_measures
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#corrective_measures> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                   <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Corrective_measures> ;
                                                                                          <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#will_be_imposed_by> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#personal_data_protection_authority> ;
                                                                                          <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#before_dictating_corrective_measures> "To have a competent technical report that allows correcting, reversing or eliminating conducts contrary to the Organic Law for the Protection of Personal Data and the regulations issued by the Authority for the Protection of Personal Data." ;
                                                                                          <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#cases_to_incur_in_corrective_measures> "In the event that controllers, persons in charge of processing personal data and certification bodies and, if applicable, third parties, are involved in the alleged commission of a minor infringement and are included in the Unified Registry of non-compliant controllers and persons in charge of processing personal data." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                      "In the event that controllers, persons in charge of the processing of personal data and certification bodies are involved in the alleged commission of a serious infringement" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                      "In the event that controllers, persons in charge of the processing of personal data and certification bodies are involved in the alleged commission of a very serious infringement" ;
                                                                                          <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#for_minor_infractions> "The Personal Data Protection Authority will directly activate the administrative sanctioning procedure, stating in the resolution both the applicable corrective measures and the sanction corresponding to the infraction committed." ;
                                                                                          <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#for_serious_infractions> "The Data Protection Authority will initially apply corrective measures. If they are not adequately complied with, sanctions for serious infringements will be imposed through the administrative sanctioning procedure." ;
                                                                                          <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#for_very_serious_offenses> "The Personal Data Protection Authority will directly activate the administrative sanctioning procedure, stating in the resolution both the applicable corrective measures and the sanction corresponding to the infraction committed." ;
                                                                                          <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#in_the_case_of_non-compliance_of> "Diposiciones prevista en la Ley Orgnánica de Protección de Datos Personales" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                 "Disobedience of the directives and guidelines issued by the Authority for the Protection of Personal Data." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                 "Infringement of data owner's rights" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                 "Violation of the fundamental principles related to the right to the protection of personal data." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                 "Violation of the regulations established by the Personal Data Protection Authority." ;
                                                                                          <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#what_will_be_the_corrective_measures> "Data deletion" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                     "The cessation of treatment, under certain conditions or time limits" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                     "The imposition of technical, legal, organizational or administrative measures to ensure proper processing of personal data" ;
                                                                                          rdfs:label "corrective measures" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#credit_data
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#credit_data> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                           <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Credit_data> ;
                                                                                  <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#description> "Data that integrate the economic behavior of natural persons, to analyze their financial capacity." ;
                                                                                  rdfs:comment "Data that integrate the economic behavior of natural persons, to analyze their financial capacity."@en ,
                                                                                               "Data that integrate the economic behavior of natural persons, to analyze their financial capacity."@es ;
                                                                                  rdfs:label "credit data" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#credit_data_processing
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#credit_data_processing> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Credit_data_processing> ;
                                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#allow_evaluate> "The commercial conduct of the data subject" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                  "The conclusion of business in general of the data subject." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                  "The data subject's ability to pay" ;
                                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#cannot_be_done_with_the_processing_of_credit_data> "The following may not be communicated" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                                     "The following may not be disseminated" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                                     "They may not have a secondary purpose" ;
                                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#credit_data_relative_with> "Banking obligations" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                             "Commercial obligations" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                             "Financial obligations" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                             "Obligaciones de carácter financiero" ;
                                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#destined> "For analysis purposes only" ;
                                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#enforceable_obligation_for_credit_data> "After five years have elapsed since the obligation has become due, the following may not be reported" ;
                                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#for_information_about> "Capital adequacy" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                         "Creditworthiness" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                         "Fulfillment of commercial obligations" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                         "Fulfillment of credit obligations" ;
                                                                                             <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#sources_from_whence_the_credit_data_was_obtained> "Public access sources" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                                    "Sources from information provided by the data owner" ;
                                                                                             rdfs:label "credit data processing" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#data_base
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#data_base> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                         <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Data_base> ;
                                                                                <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#description> "A structured data set encompasses any form, mode of creation, storage, organization, type of medium, treatment, processing, location or access, whether centralized, decentralized or distributed functionally or geographically." ;
                                                                                rdfs:comment "A structured data set encompasses any form, mode of creation, storage, organization, type of medium, treatment, processing, location or access, whether centralized, decentralized or distributed functionally or geographically."@en ,
                                                                                             "A structured data set encompasses any form, mode of creation, storage, organization, type of medium, treatment, processing, location or access, whether centralized, decentralized or distributed functionally or geographically."@es ;
                                                                                rdfs:label "data base" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#data_or_database_of_criminal_infractions
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#data_or_database_of_criminal_infractions> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                                        <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Data_or_database_of_criminal_infractions> ;
                                                                                                               <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#explanation_of_concept_of_inapplicability> "Data or databases established for the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offenses or execution of criminal sanctions, carried out by the competent state agencies in compliance with their legal functions. In any of these cases, international human rights standards and the principles of this Law must be complied with, and at least the criteria of legality, proportionality and necessity must be met." ;
                                                                                                               rdfs:label "data or database of criminal infractions" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#data_owner
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#data_owner> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                          <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Data_Owner> ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#count_with_the_following> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#rights> ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#in_case_of_impugning_the_exaccuracy_of_data_a> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#responsible_for_treatment> ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#in_case_of_suspension_of_treatment_must_resort_to> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#personal_data_protection_authority> ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#cases_in_which_the_owner_should_be_informed> "When the personal data is not obtained directly from the owner" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                   "When the personal data were obtained from a source accessible to the public" ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#control_functions> "Person whose data is processed" ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#in_case_of_no_direct_obtaining_by_the_owner> "The holder shall be informed within thirty (30) days or at the time of the first communication with the holder." ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#in_cases_of_automated_evaluations> "You may challenge automated decisions regarding the data subject's data before the data controller." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                         "You may request from the controller a detailed and reasoned explanation of the decision taken regarding the processing of your personal data." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                         "You may request from the data controller information on the types of data used and the source from which the data was obtained." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                         "You may request the evaluation criteria on the automated program." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                         "You may submit comments on the processing of your personal data." ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#obtaining_personal_data_directly_by_the_owner> "Information on how such data will be used must be provided to the data subject prior to collection, i.e., at the time the personal data is requested or collected from the data subject." ;
                                                                                 <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#type_of_person> "Natural" ;
                                                                                 rdfs:label "data owner" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#data_processing
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#data_processing> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                               <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Data_processing> ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#has_as_the_basis_of> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#legal_interest> ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#is_based_on> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#principios> ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#before_the_revocation_of_consent_is_considered_to_be_considered> "It is considered lawful, i.e. even if the data subject decides to revoke his/her consent to data processing, this does not invalidate or invalidate the data processing that was lawfully carried out prior to the revocation of consent." ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#conditions_for_legitimate_treatment> "For processing of personal data contained in publicly accessible databases" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                "Personal data involved in data processing may be used prior to entering into a contract if requested by the data subject, or during the performance of a contract to fulfill the obligations of the data controller, a person designated to handle the data, or another legally authorized party." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                "Processing personal data to satisfy a legitimate interest of the data controller or a third party. However, this legitimate interest cannot prevail over the fundamental rights of the data subjects." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                "That it is carried out by the data controller in compliance with a legal obligation." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                "That the collection, storage, use or any other operation carried out with personal data is justified in the performance of a task in the public interest or in the exercise of public powers vested in the data controller." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                "To be carried out by the data controller, by court order" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                                "To protect the vital interests of the data subject or of another natural person, such as life, health or integrity" ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#description> "Any action or set of actions performed on personal data, whether by means of fully automated, partially automated or non-automated technical processes. These actions include, but are not limited to: collecting, compiling, obtaining, recording, organizing, structuring, preserving, safeguarding, adapting, modifying, deleting, indexing, extracting, consulting, processing, using, possessing, exploiting, distributing, assigning, communicating, transferring or otherwise providing access to, collating, interconnecting, limiting, deleting, destroying and, in general, any use of personal data." ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#determine_the_compatibility> "Consideration should be given to the logical expectations that the data subject might have about the future use of his or her data, based on his or her relationship with the data controller" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                        "It should be verified that there are sufficient safeguards both in the original processing and in the proposed new processing to protect the rights and privacy of data subjects." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                        "The environment and circumstances in which the data were first obtained should be analyzed." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                        "The information provided to the data subject during the initial collection process should be taken into account." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                        "The potential impact of further processing of the data on data subjects should be analyzed" ,
                                                                                                                                                                                        "The type of personal data collected and its sensitivity must be evaluated." ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#for_different_purpose> "If they are compatible with the purposes for which they were collected." ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#low_legitimate_interest> "Only data that is strictly necessary to fulfill the purposes established in relation to the consent given and the intended processing may be processed." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                    "The Data Protection Authority has the power to request a risk report from the data controller to assess possible threats to the legitimate expectations of data subjects and their fundamental rights." ,
                                                                                                                                                                                    "The data controller must ensure that the data processing is transparent to the data subject." ;
                                                                                      <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#territorial_application_scenario> "The processing of personal data is carried out in any part of the national territory." ;
                                                                                      rdfs:comment "Any action or set of actions performed on personal data, whether by means of fully automated, partially automated or non-automated technical processes. These actions include, but are not limited to: collecting, compiling, obtaining, recording, organizing, structuring, preserving, safeguarding, adapting, modifying, deleting, indexing, extracting, consulting, processing, using, possessing, exploiting, distributing, assigning, communicating, transferring or otherwise providing access to, collating, interconnecting, limiting, deleting, destroying and, in general, any use of personal data."@en ,
                                                                                                   "Any action or set of actions performed on personal data, whether by means of fully automated, partially automated or non-automated technical processes. These actions include, but are not limited to: collecting, compiling, obtaining, recording, organizing, structuring, preserving, safeguarding, adapting, modifying, deleting, indexing, extracting, consulting, processing, using, possessing, exploiting, distributing, assigning, communicating, transferring or otherwise providing access to, collating, interconnecting, limiting, deleting, destroying and, in general, any use of personal data."@es ;
                                                                                      rdfs:label "data processing" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#data_processor
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#data_processor> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                              <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Data_Processor> ;
                                                                                     <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#is_related_to> <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#delegate> ;
                                                                                     <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#control_functions> "Processor of personal data on behalf of and for the account of a controller of personal data" ;
                                                                                     <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#delegate_comments> "Ensure that the involvement of the personal data protection officer, in all matters relating to personal data protection, is appropriate and timely." ,
                                                                                                                                                                             "Ensure that the personal data protection officer establishes direct communication with the highest executive and decision-making levels of the data processor." ,
                                                                                                                                                                             "Facilitate access to the personal data of the processing operations, as well as all the resources and elements necessary to guarantee the correct and free performance of its functions." ,
                                                                                                                                                                             "They may not dismiss or sanction the personal data protection officer for the proper performance of his or her duties." ,
                                                                                                                                                                             "Train and update the personal data protection officer on the subject, in accordance with the technical regulations issued by the Personal Data Protection Authority." ;
                                                                                     <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#minor_infractions> "Failure to allow or cooperate with audits or inspections carried out by the data controller or other auditor authorized by the Personal Data Protection Authority" ,
                                                                                                                                                                             "Failure to comply with the corrective measures ordered by the Personal Data Protection Authority." ,
                                                                                                                                                                             "Failure to cooperate with the data controller to enable the data controller to respond adequately to requests from data subjects" ,
                                                                                                                                                                             "Failure to provide the data controller with all the information necessary to comply with the obligations established by the Organic Law on Personal Data Protection and the corresponding regulations." ;
                                                                                     <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#nature_of_the_entity> "Public or Private" ;
                                                                                     <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#obligations> "Allowing audits and inspections by accredited auditors" ,
                                                                                                                                                                       "Comply with any other obligation established by applicable regulations or other Ecuadorian laws." ,
                                                                                                                                                                       "Conduct security adequacy assessments prior to the processing of personal data." ,
                                                                                                                                                                       "Designate a Data Protection Officer when necessary." ,
                                                                                                                                                                       "Develop customized data protection policies" ,
                                                                                                                                                                       "Ensure that data processors comply with regulations and best practices." ,
                                                                                                                                                                       "Establish confidentiality agreements with personnel and data controllers." ,
                                                                                                                                                                       "Implement administrative, technical and legal measures to guarantee the proper treatment of data" ,
                                                                                                                                                                       "Maintain the National Registry of Personal Data Protection up to date." ,
                                                                                                                                                                       "Notifying the Personal Data Protection Authority and the data owner of violations of the security measures implemented for the processing of personal data in accordance with the procedure established for this purpose." ,
                                                                                                                                                                       "Periodically evaluate the effectiveness of the administrative, technical and legal measures adopted." ,
                                                                                                                                                                       "Take the necessary technological, physical, administrative, organizational and legal measures to prevent, deter, reduce, mitigate and control identified risks and breaches." ,
                                                                                                                                                                       "Treat personal data in accordance with the Organic Law on Personal Data Protection and relevant regulations." ,
                                                                                                                                                                       "Use risk analysis and management methodologies adapted to the particularities of data processing and the parties involved." ;
                                                                                     <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#serious_infractions> "Failure to comply with corrective measures or partial or defective compliance with them, provided that a sanction for a minor infraction has been applied beforehand for this reason." ,
                                                                                                                                                                               "Failure to implement mechanisms designed to maintain the confidentiality, integrity, availability and resilience of personal data" ,
                                                                                                                                                                               "Failure to implement preventive and corrective measures in the security of personal data in order to avoid violations." ,
                                                                                                                                                                               "Failure to notify the data controller of any breach of security of personal data in accordance with the Organic Law on Personal Data Protection or with unjustified delay." ,
                                                                                                                                                                               "Failure to process personal data in accordance with the provisions of the contract with the data controller" ,
                                                                                                                                                                               "Failure to sign contracts containing confidentiality and appropriate treatment of personal data clauses with the personnel in charge of the treatment of personal data or whoever has knowledge of the personal data." ,
                                                                                                                                                                               "Not to delete the personal data transferred or communicated to the person in charge of the processing of personal data, once its assignment has been completed." ,
                                                                                                                                                                               "Processing personal data without respecting the principles and rights established in the Organic Law for the Protection of Personal Data, its regulations and the rules issued by the Authority for the Protection of Personal Data." ;
                                                                                     <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#type_authority> "Public" ;
                                                                                     <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#type_of_organism_participation> "Alone or together with others" ;
                                                                                     <http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#type_of_person> "Natural or Legal" ;
                                                                                     rdfs:label "data processor" .


